      "text": "We need sum of first 40 digits after decimal of \\(1/1111\\).\n\nFirst, note \\(1111 = 11 \\times 101\\). But maybe easier: \\(1/1111 = 0.\\overline{0009}\\)? Let's check.\n\nActually \\(1/1111\\):  \n\\(1111 \\times 9 = 9999\\), so \\(1/1111 = 9/9999 = 0.\\overline{0009}\\). Yes, because \\(9/9999 = 0.\\overline{0009}\\) repeating every 4 digits.\n\nLet's verify: \\(0.\\overline{0009} = 9/(10^4-1) = 9/9999 = 1/1111\\). Correct.\n\nSo decimal is \\(0.000900090009\\ldots\\) repeating block \"0009\".\n\nFirst 40 digits: 40/4 = 10 full blocks of \"0009\".\n\nEach block sum = 0+0+0+9 = 9.  \n10 blocks sum = 90.\n\nThe answer is 90. \n\nThe answer is 90.",
